course: dictionary
lesson: 5495
title: Lava: melted rock
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lava is hot, melted rock that flows out of a volcano. Melted means the rock has become so hot that it runs like a liquid, similar to water or syrup. Lava is an uncountable noun, so we say some lava, not a lava.
explain: Look at the context: «Lava from a volcano is rock so hot that it has melted into a liquid; when it cools it freezes back into solid rock.» The words cools and freezes back tell you what happens next: the lava gets cooler and turns hard again.
explain: The same word can mean two things. Lava can be the hot, flowing rock, or the solid rock that forms when it cools. Read the clues around it to see which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Lava is hot, melted rock that flows out of a volcano.
fact: When lava cools, it hardens into solid rock.
fact: «Basalt» is a dark, fine-grained rock made from runny lava, and it is the most common rock of the ocean floor.
fact: «Glass» can form in nature when lightning strikes sand, or when lava cools very fast.
fact: In games, «the floor is lava» means you must not touch the floor.
exercise: «Lava from a volcano is rock so hot that it has melted into a liquid.» What is lava? | *Hot, melted rock that flows out of a volcano | A cold, hard stone found in rivers | A tall mountain with snow on top | A type of cloud that floats over the sea
exercise: «Nature makes glass too, when lightning strikes sand or lava cools very fast.» What does this tell you about lava? | *Lava can cool so fast that it can turn into glass | Lava is only found in video games | Lava always stays liquid forever | Lava is made of glass already
exercise: In «runny lava», what does runny mean? | *Flowing easily, like a liquid | Full of holes | Very sticky and slow | Covered in ice
test: In the game «the floor is lava», what must you do? | Paint the floor red | Dance on the floor | *Keep your feet off the floor | Walk slowly across the floor
test: Which statement is true? | Lava is solid rock before it comes out of a volcano | *Lava is hot, melted rock that flows out of a volcano | Lava is cold water from the sea | Lava is a sweet-smelling gas
exam: According to the text, where is basalt the most common rock? | In the middle of a desert | Inside a glass bottle | In the snow at the top of ski slopes | *On the ocean floor
